{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-doc-js","path":"/docs/data_usage_telemetry/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"frontmatter":{"title":"Data Usage and Telemetry"},"html":"<h1 id=\"data-usage-and-telemetry-in-theia\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#data-usage-and-telemetry-in-theia\" aria-label=\"data usage and telemetry in theia permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Data Usage and Telemetry in Theia</h1>\n<p>Eclipse Theia and Theia IDE are fully open-source projects. This means you can review the source code to verify exactly how the application behaves. Transparency is a core principle—no hidden services or undisclosed data collection take place.</p>\n<h2 id=\"no-built-in-telemetry\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#no-built-in-telemetry\" aria-label=\"no built in telemetry permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>No Built-in Telemetry</h2>\n<p>The Theia IDE itself does not include built-in telemetry. It does not automatically collect or transmit user activity, project details, or code.</p>\n<p>However, tool builders who create custom products based on Theia can choose to add their own telemetry systems. If you are using a customized Theia-based product, you should consult that product's specific privacy policy and documentation for details about its data collection practices.</p>\n<h2 id=\"automatic-network-connections\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#automatic-network-connections\" aria-label=\"automatic network connections permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Automatic Network Connections</h2>\n<p>While Theia IDE does not include telemetry, there are two automatic checks made during normal operation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Update Check for Theia IDE</strong>: The IDE may query the download servers to see if a newer version of Theia IDE is available.</li>\n<li><strong>Extension Update Check</strong>: The IDE may query Open VSX to determine whether newer versions of installed extensions are available.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These checks are limited to update metadata and do not transmit user code or workspace data.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ai-features-and-data-handling\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#ai-features-and-data-handling\" aria-label=\"ai features and data handling permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>AI Features and Data Handling</h2>\n<p>Theia AI and related AI features are opt-in. If you do not enable them, no AI-related data is sent anywhere.</p>\n<p>When Theia AI features are enabled:</p>\n<h3 id=\"manual-activation\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#manual-activation\" aria-label=\"manual activation permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Manual Activation</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Most AI interactions (e.g., chat, code transformation) are triggered explicitly by the user.</li>\n<li>Automatic code completion is separately opt-in to prevent accidental transmission of code.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"transparency-in-data-transfer\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#transparency-in-data-transfer\" aria-label=\"transparency in data transfer permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Transparency in Data Transfer</h3>\n<p>You can inspect exactly what data is sent to AI providers using:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The Output view</li>\n<li>The AI History view</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"permissions-control\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#permissions-control\" aria-label=\"permissions control permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Permissions Control</h3>\n<p>Theia includes an optional permission system for tool calls. When enabled, the Chat UI will request explicit approval for file system or other tool access.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Note</strong>: Autocomplete does not use tool calls, so it should be managed carefully in sensitive environments.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"third-party-providers\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#third-party-providers\" aria-label=\"third party providers permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Third-Party Providers</h2>\n<p>Theia integrates with the official SDKs for each AI provider (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic, Google). Theia itself does not send your data anywhere other than the chosen provider's API endpoint.</p>\n<p>What the provider does with your data depends on their own policies. Theia cannot inspect or control additional behavior of:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>AI model providers</li>\n<li>Any MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers you integrate</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"optional-integrations\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#optional-integrations\" aria-label=\"optional integrations permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Optional Integrations</h2>\n<h3 id=\"scanoss-integration\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#scanoss-integration\" aria-label=\"scanoss integration permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>SCANOSS Integration</h3>\n<p>Theia offers an integration with SCANOSS for code analysis and compliance checks. This is also opt-in and only sends code to SCANOSS when explicitly enabled.</p>\n<h2 id=\"key-takeaways\" style=\"position:relative;\"><a href=\"#key-takeaways\" aria-label=\"key takeaways permalink\" class=\"anchor before\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" width=\"16\"><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z\"></path></svg></a>Key Takeaways</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>No telemetry in Theia and Theia IDE by default</li>\n<li>AI features are opt-in and transparent</li>\n<li>Only minimal automatic network activity (update checks)</li>\n</ul>","fields":{"slug":"data_usage_telemetry"}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"data_usage_telemetry"}},"staticQueryHashes":["2468095761"],"slicesMap":{}}